5. Authentication System
Authentication JWT based hai.

Register
POST /api/auth/register

User data:

{
  "name": "John",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "phone": "1234567890",
  "password": "password"
}

Backend:

Existing email check karta hai.
Password bcrypt se hash karta hai.
User create karta hai.
Verification token create karta hai.
Verification email bhejta hai.
6. Email Verification
GET /api/auth/verify/:token

Verification successful hone par:

user.isVerified = true;

ho jata hai.

7. Login
POST /api/auth/login

Login ke waqt:

Email find hota hai.
Email verification check hota hai.
Password compare hota hai.
Access token generate hota hai.
Refresh token generate hota hai.
Refresh token database me save hota hai.
Refresh token HTTP-only cookie me save hota hai.
Response me access token milta hai.

Example:

{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Login successful",
  "accessToken": "...",
  "user": {
    "id": "...",
    "name": "...",
    "email": "..."
  }
}

8. Logout
POST /api/auth/logout

Refresh token database se remove hota hai aur cookie clear hoti hai.

9. Refresh Access Token
POST /api/auth/refresh

Refresh token HTTP-only cookie se liya jata hai.

Naya access token generate hota hai.

10. Forgot Password
POST /api/auth/forgot-password

Password reset token generate hota hai aur email bheja jata hai.

11. Reset Password
POST /api/auth/reset-password/:token

New password bcrypt se hash hota hai.

Refresh token invalidate kar diya jata hai.

12. Authentication Middleware
Backend ka authentication middleware:

authMiddleware

Authorization header se token leta hai:

Authorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN

JWT verify karta hai aur database se user find karta hai.

Phir:

req.user = user;

set karta hai.

13. Admin Middleware
Admin ke liye existing middleware:

const adminMiddleware = async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    if (!req.user) {
      return res.status(401).json({
        success: false,
        message: "Authentication required",
      });
    }

    if (req.user.role !== "admin") {
      return res.status(403).json({
        success: false,
        message: "Admin access only",
      });
    }

    next();
  } catch (error) {
    return res.status(500).json({
      success: false,
      message: error.message,
    });
  }
};

Flow:

Admin Login
    ↓
/api/auth/login
    ↓
JWT
    ↓
Frontend stores access token
    ↓
Admin API request
    ↓
authMiddleware
    ↓
adminMiddleware
    ↓
Admin Controller

Backend me separate admin login endpoint nahi banana hai.

14. API Key Middleware
API key middleware:

x-api-key

header se API key leta hai.

Key ko SHA-256 hash karta hai.

Database me keyHash find karta hai.

Inactive key reject hoti hai.

Valid key hone par:

req.apiKey

aur:

req.emailProject

set hote hain.

Usage count bhi increment hota hai.

